---Activate a signing key
---
---Activate a pending signing key so the issuer starts signing with it.
---
---`POST /v1/kms/issuers/{issuerId}/keys/{keyId}/activate`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input vercel.kms.ActivateKmsSigningKeyRequest
---@return vercel.kms.ActivateKmsSigningKeyResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:activate_kms_signing_key(input) end

---Create an issuer
---
---Create a new KMS issuer for the authenticated team, or for the team or organization identified by a Connect policy token. An issuer owns the asymmetric signing keys used to sign tokens and messages.
---
---`POST /v1/kms/issuers`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input vercel.kms.CreateKmsIssuerRequest
---@return vercel.kms.CreateKmsIssuerResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_kms_issuer(input) end

---Create an issuer policy
---
---Attach a policy to a KMS issuer that grants a project's deployments permission to sign with it.
---
---`POST /v1/kms/issuers/{issuerId}/policies`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input vercel.kms.CreateKmsIssuerPolicyRequest
---@return vercel.kms.CreateKmsIssuerPolicyResponseBody? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_kms_issuer_policy(input) end

---Create a signing key
---
---Create a new signing key for a KMS issuer. Depending on the activation mode, the key is activated automatically once its public key has propagated, or manually via the activate endpoint.
---
---`POST /v1/kms/issuers/{issuerId}/keys`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input vercel.kms.CreateKmsSigningKeyRequest
---@return vercel.kms.CreateKmsSigningKeyResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_kms_signing_key(input) end

---Delete an issuer
---
---Delete a KMS issuer and its signing keys.
---
---`DELETE /v1/kms/issuers/{issuerId}`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input vercel.kms.DeleteKmsIssuerRequest
---@return vercel.kms.DeleteKmsIssuerResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_kms_issuer(input) end

---Delete an issuer policy
---
---Remove a policy from a KMS issuer.
---
---`DELETE /v1/kms/issuers/{issuerId}/policies/{kind}/{policyKey}`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input vercel.kms.DeleteKmsIssuerPolicyRequest
---@return vercel.kms.DeleteKmsIssuerPolicyResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_kms_issuer_policy(input) end

---Get an issuer
---
---Retrieve a single KMS issuer by its ID. Accepts a team or organization bearer token, or an OIDC token authorized by one of the issuer's policies (e.g. a connex-grant token). The OIDC path returns the issuer without policies, since a policy token only proves signing access, not management access.
---
---`GET /v1/kms/issuers/{issuerId}`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input vercel.kms.GetKmsIssuerRequest
---@return vercel.kms.GetKmsIssuerResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_kms_issuer(input) end

---List issuers
---
---Retrieve the paginated KMS issuers that belong to the authenticated team or organization (`orgId`).
---
---`GET /v1/kms/issuers`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input? vercel.kms.ListKmsIssuersRequest
---@return vercel.kms.ListKmsIssuersResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_kms_issuers(input) end

---Revoke a signing key
---
---Immediately revoke a signing key that is already scheduled for revocation.
---
---`POST /v1/kms/issuers/{issuerId}/keys/{keyId}/revoke`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input vercel.kms.RevokeKmsSigningKeyRequest
---@return vercel.kms.RevokeKmsSigningKeyResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:revoke_kms_signing_key(input) end

---Sign a message
---
---Sign a raw message with a KMS issuer's active signing key. Authenticate the request with a Vercel OIDC token in the `Authorization: Bearer` header; the issuer's policies decide which workloads are allowed to sign. The response `signature` is standard-base64 of the raw signature over the decoded message bytes. `keyId`, `algorithm`, and `fingerprint` identify the signing key in the issuer's JWKS.
---
---`POST /v1/kms/issuers/{issuerId}/sign/message`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input vercel.kms.SignKmsMessageRequest
---@return vercel.kms.SignKmsMessageResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:sign_kms_message(input) end

---Sign a token
---
---Sign a JWT with a KMS issuer's active signing key. Authenticate the request with a Vercel OIDC token in the `Authorization: Bearer` header; the issuer's policies decide which workloads are allowed to sign. `keyId`, `algorithm`, and `fingerprint` identify the signing key in the issuer's JWKS.
---
---`POST /v1/kms/issuers/{issuerId}/sign/token`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input vercel.kms.SignKmsTokenRequest
---@return vercel.kms.SignKmsTokenResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:sign_kms_token(input) end

